<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Activity theme. Compose owns everything visible; this exists so the window
  has a background and a status-bar treatment before the first frame, which is
  what stops a white flash on a dark device.

  WHY THE BASE IS NOT A DayNight THEME.

  `android:Theme.Material.DayNight` does not exist. The platform ships
  `Theme.Material` and `Theme.Material.Light` from API 21, and the only
  platform DayNight family is `Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight`, added in API 29.
  Referencing the non-existent name failed the resource link outright:

      AAPT: error: resource android:style/Theme.Material.DayNight.NoActionBar
      not found.

  `minSdk` is 26, so the DayNight base cannot be unconditional. This file is
  the API 26-28 form and `values-v29/themes.xml` overrides it with the real
  DayNight theme where the platform has one. Both set the same three
  attributes, so the pre-first-frame appearance is identical; only the
  light/dark following differs, and it differs exactly where the platform
  gained the ability.

  The alternative was an AppCompat dependency for `Theme.AppCompat.DayNight`.
  Not taken: the app is Compose, has no AppCompat dependency today, and adding
  one to name a theme is a dependency-surface decision under ADR-0018 DP-3 for
  a cosmetic gain on three API levels.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.TwinVPN" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">?android:attr/colorBackground</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">?android:attr/colorBackground</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">?android:attr/colorBackground</item>
    </style>
</resources>
